Z||000000||Taijiguy||05-05-2000||03:14 PM||||OK dudes, not to be boring...I know this topic has been addressed a hundered times, but I can't find the info anywhere, so I'll ask. <BR>I'm considering a swap in my 85GT from the 2.8 to a 3.8. What's the hassles in that switch? I'd also like to move up from the 4 speed to a Getrag 5 speed. I've thought about just normally aspirating it to avoid all the computer headaches, with maybe a supercharger. All that aside, what am I going to have to contend with doing this swap from a mechanical standpoint, such as: <P>Engine to trans mounting<BR>Shifter issues <BR>Fuel pump supply<BR>Cooling<P>Anything else come to mind?<P>Thanks all. Please forgive the redundancy!<P>Later<P>||||reg||5
Z||000001||Phil||05-05-2000||04:35 PM||||Check <A HREF="http://www.americancustomeng.com" TARGET=_blank>www.americancustomeng.com</A>    You need to use the computer from the 3800 and if you go with the stick shift a custom flywheel also. The wiring is a pain in the shorts as is a exhaust system. Figure $5k++ for the job. Normally aspirated with a supercharger????<BR>Phil S/C 3800||||reg||1
